{
  "$about": "Image, video and voice models the Models page can download, beside the chat GGUFs in model-catalog.json. Image and video models with a `workflow` run in ComfyUI, which Rosalena starts on demand (src/comfy-runner.mjs) with the graph in data/comfy-workflows/<workflow>.json filled from `defaults`; `companions` are the extra files (text encoder, VAE) that download with the model. Whisper files run in whisper.cpp (src/voice-runner.mjs), which the first Whisper download brings with it. Text-to-speech entries are download-only: Rosalena has no speaking feature yet. Each file is one download from Hugging Face; `bytes` and `sha256` were read from Hugging Face's own headers for that exact file on 2026-11-03, and the download checks both again before it keeps the file.",
  "$fit": "`needGiB` is an estimate of the video memory the model wants while it runs at its default size (the weights plus working memory at 1024 px for images and 480p-720p for short video clips), not a measurement. ComfyUI can keep part of a model in system RAM when the card is short, which works but is slower: the page calls that 'tight'. `cpuOk` marks models that run fine on the processor alone.",
  "$folders": "Downloads go to ~/.rosalena/models/<kind>/<folder>/, where <folder> is the ComfyUI models subfolder the file belongs in (checkpoints, diffusion_models, text_encoders, vae). A ComfyUI that Rosalena starts is pointed at both folders with --extra-model-paths-config; one started elsewhere needs the same lines in its own extra_model_paths.yaml.",
  "version": 1,
  "updated": "2026-11-03",
